What:  Release designer 0.48.0: bump, calibrate the kit (codex, GLM-5.3), cut, commit, tag designer-v0.48.0 locally, browser tier on the pool (4 shards), core tier, push
       Release 0.48.0 (minor), as you asked on 2026-11-24. Three changes, all from Greenfield's maps:
       - a lane's documentation is kept on save (T-1500): every earlier version dropped it on every save, silently
         (Greenfield keeps the lane's owner role there);
       - a selected step's, gateway's, event's or lane's documentation is shown in the panel, read-only (T-1492);
       - each phase row is named at its left ('Fase', 'Fase in Salesforce') (T-1498).
       What a save writes changes only for maps whose lanes carry documentation (now kept). Notes: docs/releases/RELEASE-NOTES-0.48.0.md.
       Steps 2-3 calibrate the kit with live reviewers (a few minutes each, model time); if one does not PASS, nothing is
       released and the agent brings it to you. Step 7 tags locally. Step 8 runs the browser tier on the pool, split in 4
       (about 9-10 minutes; your option 1 for 0.45.0), and stops the job if red or without a result, with nothing pushed.
       Step 9 runs the core tier (about 20 minutes, or cached); step 10 pushes bleeding-edge and the tag. Answer y at every
       step. Afterwards the agent tells AEF and Greenfield.
