  1. Bump VERSION and APP_VERSION to 0.48.0 and commit (parity checked)
  2. Calibrate with codex (OpenAI): build the 0.48.0 kit, loop.sh --calibrate, record the result (outward)
  3. Calibrate with GLM-5.3 (Z.AI, opencode): build the 0.48.0 kit, loop.sh --calibrate, record the result (outward)
  4. Release gate: the 0.48.0 kit carries a PASS calibration of its exact bytes (outward)
  5. Cut release 0.48.0: scripts/release-designer.sh (render gate ON, announce ON; writes dist/) (outward)
  6. Commit dist/aef-workflow-designer-0.48.0.html, dist/aef-authoring-kit-0.48.0, dist/MANIFEST.yaml and the calibration record (outward)
  7. Tag designer-v0.48.0 (annotated) on the release commit, locally only (outward)
  8. Browser tier on the pool, 4 shards (T1467_POOL_ONLY=1; about 7-12 min): stops here if red or no result, nothing pushed (outward)
  9. Core tier (about 20 minutes, or cached), so the push finds it green (outward)
  10. Push bleeding-edge and designer-v0.48.0 to origin (outward)

